[E0437] Error: `c` would borrow a temporary
    ╭─[ err/443_a_c_string_that_outlives_its_bytes/main.wip:15:10 ]
    │
 15 │     val c = String::of(name).toCstring()
    │             ────────┬─────┬─────────────
    │                     ╰───────────────────── a temporary, dropped at the end of the statement
    │                           │
    │                           ╰─────────────── a C string is kept here
    │
    │ Help: keep the `String` in a variable, and make the C string from it where it is used
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows, which must live as long as it does
────╯
[E0436] Error: `c` is used after `s`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/443_a_c_string_that_outlives_its_bytes/main.wip:23:16 ]
    │
 21 │     val c = s.toCstring()
    │         ┬
    │         ╰── `c` borrows `s`
 22 │     s.push(" there")
    │     ┬
    │     ╰── `s` passed as `&var` here
 23 │     return strlen(c)
    │                   ┬
    │                   ╰── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `c` before `s` changes, or make the C string again after the change
    │
    │ Note: a C string made from a `String` points into its bytes, so those must not change while the C string is still used
────╯
